ProfanityMeter's Privacy Policy

Last updated: July 26th, 2026

1. Summary

ProfanityMeter ("the Bot") does not maintain its own database of your
messages, message content, or word counts. It queries Discord's API live.
It does not persist search results after the command finishes running.

 2. What Data the Bot Accesses

To function, the Bot receives (via Discord's API, under Discord's own
Message Content Intent):
- Your Discord user ID, to identify which messages are yours.
- The list of servers ("guilds") the Bot and you are both members of.
- Search result counts from Discord's guild
  message search endpoint, filtered to messages you authored.

3. What the Bot Stores

Nothing. The Bot does not run a database and does not log,
save, or export your message content, search results, or word counts
anywhere. Query results exist only in memory for the duration of the
command and are discarded once the response is sent.

Standard operational logs (e.g. errors, which command was run, by which
user ID, for debugging uptime issues) may be kept temporarily by the bot
host but do not include message content.

4. Data Sharing

The Bot does not sell, share, or transmit your data to any third party.
All processing happens between the Bot and Discord's API.

7. Changes to This Policy

This policy may be updated as the Bot's functionality changes. If the Bot
ever begins storing data (e.g. a caching layer added later), this policy
will be updated to disclose that before the change ships.

